We will need to know the values of $g(1)$ and $g(3)$ to find the slope.

$\begin{align}
g(1)&=\dfrac{2}{1+3}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{1}{2}
\\\\\\
g(3)&=\dfrac{2}{3+3}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{1}{3}
\\\\\\
\dfrac{g(3)-g(1)}{3-1}&=\dfrac{\dfrac{1}{3}-\dfrac{1}{2}}{2}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{\left(- \dfrac{1}{6}\right)}{2}
\\\\
&=-\dfrac{1}{12}
\end{align}$
